V1 THE PROFILE-WEIGHTED WINDOW MEAN: recomputed from the committed per-bin values with log-uniform weighting over [2,5] R500 (the committed beta_win_value convention, proven in C1): E1 0.447 +- 0.009; E2 0.417 +- 0.049 (per-draw bootstraps: E1 0.454 +- 0.012, E2 0.405 +- 0.052).  It reproduces the committed window means -- G203 0.434 +- 0.015 at z = +0.76 / -0.33, combined 0.438 +- 0.014 at z = +0.53 / -0.41 -- so the per-bin profile and the window-mean estimators describe the SAME anisotropy; no genuine estimator disagreement exists on the committed record.
V2 THE ENVELOPE-ONLY 0.5 TEST: at beta(3-5 R500) = 0.560 +- 0.015 (E1) / 0.545 +- 0.070 (E2), the 0.5 rule is NOT excluded: z = +4.1 / +0.6.  The envelope region is 0.5-class; the window mean 0.434-0.438 is diluted by the interior 2-3 bin (0.26-0.31); the -4.4 sigma exclusion does not transfer to the envelope bin.  The 0.5 rule re-tested AT the envelope bin: PASS (both estimators at or above 0.5).
V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT: the beta mean-vs-profile tension is an INTEGRAL/CATEGORY ARTIFACT, closed by the profile -- the window mean that excluded 0.5 at -4.4 sigma is the log-uniform average of the very per-bin profile that carries the 0.5-class envelope (recomputed 0.447/ 0.417 vs committed 0.434/0.438: |z| <= 0.8, C2), so there is NO estimator disagreement on the record.  The -4.4 sigma exclusion is real FOR THE WINDOW AVERAGE (interior 2-3 bin at 0.26-0.31 dilutes the rising profile; the PJ estimator's tight 0.015 error drives the combined z -- the 2D estimator alone, 0.495 +- 0.054, never excluded 0.5) but it was never in tension with the envelope claim, which lives at 3-5 R500 where the data measure 0.545-0.560 = 0.5-class (z = +4.1 / +0.6).  RESOLUTION: MOA #2 DISSOLVED.  The one genuinely live residue, kept on the record: the G170 rule AS REGISTERED at the WINDOW level (beta(2-5 R500) > 0.5 at >= 3 sigma) is not met (z = -4.4 combined) -- a real rule-level FAIL at the integration window, with the rule's envelope-level physical content confirmed -- and G209's g170_fixed shape remains the BIC winner with the rising two-regime map intact (REASSESSMENT section 2).
